From: Ali Zain <alizain@zainiumdynamics.tech>
Subject: [PATCH] zainium: system paths under /overlayer/syshub

Config, data, state and helper paths point into /overlayer/syshub:
Zainium has no /etc, /usr or /var at the root. Image and container
tools keep the stock paths, since they read other systems, and so do
the checks that move a legacy /var/run/ path in a unit to /run.
---
diff --git a/src/analyze/analyze-unit-shell.c b/src/analyze/analyze-unit-shell.c
index 98dc474..625d370 100644
--- a/src/analyze/analyze-unit-shell.c
+++ b/src/analyze/analyze-unit-shell.c
@@ -106,8 +106,8 @@ int verb_unit_shell(int argc, char *argv[], uintptr_t _data, void *userdata) {
                                 log_debug_errno(errno, "Failed to execute '/bin/bash', ignoring: %m");
                         }
 
-                        if (!streq(DEFAULT_USER_SHELL, "/bin/sh")) {
-                                (void) execl("/bin/sh", "-sh", NULL);
+                        if (!streq(DEFAULT_USER_SHELL, "/overlayer/syshub/bin/bash")) {
+                                (void) execl("/overlayer/syshub/bin/bash", "-sh", NULL);
                                 log_debug_errno(errno, "Failed to execute '/bin/sh', ignoring: %m");
                         }
 
